    "body": "This is following the format for e.g. [set up a `ReadableStream`](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#readablestream-set-up). The intention is that you created this object without running the [`new ReadableStreamDefaultReader()` constructor](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#default-reader-constructor).\n\nThis is needed because (if I understand correctly) the IDL machinery does not automatically call the \"super constructor\" when you define a constructor for a subclass. If we're wrong about that, then we may want to revise all of our \"set up\" algorithms. 😅",
    "created_at": "2026-04-21T20:47:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-21T20:47:20Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/whatwg/streams/pull/1370#discussion_r3120219594",
